In that-- in this cellar, mine little nephew died, the little baby. Because right away, we did not have-- she didn't have any milk. And you couldn't buy any milk. You couldn't buy nothing. So I tried to get out from the ghetto to organize some food.

And that where it start with the tram-- street trams. The motorists from the street trams, they were-- they were very sympathetic to us. And they helped us a lot by slowing down the train when they went through the ghetto. So we jumped out. And we jumped in. And on the [? Irish ?] side and the Polish side, we jumped out.

